STOP RESULT
classification=DISSIPATION_PATH_DEFECT_IDENTIFIED

The production trace finds that the live direct target-d=4 RHS omits
Kreiss-Oliger dissipation. Per the D10 stop rule, the fixture-only tangent
map, dominant-mode iterations, and medium-resolution variants were not built
or run. No production repair is made in this stage.

ACTUAL PRODUCTION CALL PATH
1. Chombo LevelRK4::advance evaluates four RHS stages and performs seven
   updateODE calls per complete step (four accumulated-solution updates and
   three stage predictors).
2. GRAMRLevel::evalRHS calls soln.exchange(m_exchange_copier), performs any
   coarse interpolation (dormant at level zero), calls the black-string
   radial-only fillBdyGhosts, then calls specificEvalRHS.
3. BlackStringToyLevel::specificEvalRHS loops BlackStringLive::RHSCompute over
   valid cells, then applies the project outer valid-surface RHS to Interval
   0..17 when physical radial boundaries are active.
4. GRAMRLevel then calls locked BoundaryConditions::fill_rhs_boundaries for
   its configured nonperiodic RHS ghosts.
5. GRAMRLevel::updateODE performs soln.plus(rhs,dt,m_grown_grids), invokes
   BlackStringToyLevel::specificUpdateODE, and refills boundaries.
6. specificUpdateODE applies hidden-aware determinant normalization,
   weighted trace removal, and chi/lapse floors on valid cells after every RK
   update.

GRID DERIVATIVES AND ADVECTION
source=code/BlackStringToy/BlackStringLive.hpp:70-99
operator=locked FourthOrderDerivatives
grid_dimensions=CH_SPACEDIM=2
radial_direction=0
compact_direction=1
component_loop=0..17

For each stored slot, make_pointwise_input explicitly obtains only
m_in_stride[0] and m_in_stride[1], then computes:
  d_x  = (f[-2]-8f[-1]+8f[+1]-f[+2])/(12 dx)
  d_z  = the same stencil on the compact stride
  d_xx = (-f[-2]+16f[-1]-30f[0]+16f[+1]-f[+2])/(12 dx^2)
  d_zz = the same stencil on the compact stride
  d_xz = the locked tensor-product fourth-order mixed stencil

The live grid is isotropic, so the one m_dx supplied to the locked kernels is
the radial and compact spacing. Shift advection is assembled for every stored
slot as beta^x*d_x U + beta^z*d_z U and mapped to the target tensor row.

TARGET DIMENSION AND HIDDEN ACCESS
source=code/BlackStringToy/BlackStringTargetCCZ4Pointwise.hpp:340-653
target_dimension=4
gridded_dimension=2

Physical loops over target_dimension operate only on already-expanded tensor
objects. The two hidden directions are supplied by algebraic modified-cartoon
relations in set_scalar_jet, set_vector_jet, and
add_hidden_tensor_derivatives. No hidden direction selects a Cell stride,
IntVect coordinate, or grid pointer. The active derivative path therefore
contains no direction-2/3 grid access.

