DISSIPATION TRACE
locked_source=external/GRChombo/Source/CCZ4/CCZ4RHS.impl.hpp:39-54
locked_stencil=external/GRChombo/Source/BoxUtils/FourthOrderDerivatives.hpp:360-414
live_direct_source=code/BlackStringToy/BlackStringTargetCCZ4Pointwise.hpp:227-237,728-736
parameter_source=code/BlackStringToy/SimulationParameters.hpp:13-72

Locked CCZ4RHS::compute performs:
  load vars
  bulk diff1/diff2/advection
  rhs_equation
  m_deriv.add_dissipation(rhs,current_cell,m_sigma)
  store rhs

The live LockedRHSAccess instead exposes rhs_equation and evaluate_direct calls
that protected equation directly. CCZ4RHS::compute is never invoked.
LockedRHSAccess also constructs its otherwise unused base with a_sigma=0.0.
The project SimulationParameters derives from ChomboParameters, not
SimulationParametersBase, and neither loads nor stores sigma. The upstream
SimulationParametersBase default sigma=0.1 and the obsolete stage-2 smoke
file sigma=0.3 have no ownership of the live BlackStringToy RHS.

effective_KO_coefficient=0
effective_KO_component_coverage=0/18
effective_radial_KO_coverage=0/18
effective_compact_KO_coverage=0/18

The inactive locked KO term is the seven-point stencil
  sigma/dx * [1,-6,15,-20,15,-6,1]/64.
At the radial Nyquist mode its symbol is -sigma/dx, so its sign is damping;
its scaling is 1/dx; enum_mapping covers every variable in the supplied Vars.
There is no active sign, spacing, or partial-component error because the term
is absent from the live path.

The generic no-direction add_dissipation overload uses target-wide FOR(dir)
and then m_in_stride[dir]. Under CH_SPACEDIM=2 and DEFAULT_TENSOR_DIM=4 it
would request nonexistent hidden grid strides. Therefore replacing the direct
call with generic CCZ4RHS::compute is not an admissible repair. A future
repair needs explicit CH_SPACEDIM direction ownership for the reduced 18-slot
state.

