Cleanup follows each updateODE, not evalRHS. It sees the just-updated valid
state, normalizes the full d=4 determinant with the two hidden hww copies,
removes the weighted d=4 A trace, stores one hww/Aww copy, applies positivity
floors, and is followed by a radial ghost refresh.

